But before that, hit the like and subscribe button. Some years ago, I was asked to reimagine performance

10
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:23,780
management in my organization a privilege for me because we employed hundreds of thousands of people.

11
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:31,700
And the question I asked was, what creates great individual and team performance? And in looking

12
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:38,060
for answers, we researched companies that had outperformed their competitors for a long period of

13
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:43,980
time. We went outside the corporate realm and actually looked at elite sports teams and defense

14
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:53,100
organizations and then sat down to glean learnings. What we actually found stunned us. We learned that

15
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:59,660
performance management systems actually had no correlation with organizational performance. Instead,

16
00:02:00,380 --> 00:02:10,780
we found six universal truths of performance. Here they are. First, when we do what we are great at and

17
00:02:10,780 --> 00:02:18,540
love to do. Meaning when we apply our strengths, our skills, our passion at what we do every single day.

18
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:27,260
Second, when we focus on the vital few priorities, not our entire goal sheets, not all of our KPIs,

19
00:02:27,820 --> 00:02:35,180
but just the five or seven things that we need to get right. And when we do that, it creates a disproportionate

20
00:02:35,180 --> 00:02:44,060
impact. Third, performance is a team sport. When we complement each other's strengths and skills,

21
00:02:45,420 --> 00:02:53,500
when we are focused on the same mission, and when we have a high trust equation amongst each others.

22
00:02:54,140 --> 00:02:57,500
Those are highly engaged teams that create great performance.

23
00:02:57,500 --> 00:03:08,060
feedback is vital to performance. But feedback is not an event. So when we have feedback at the end of

24
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:14,380
the year or once in six months, none of us can actually look back and improve our performance

25
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:21,180
retrospectively. But if we get feedback in the moment, if we get coaching in the moment, each one of us can

26
00:03:21,180 --> 00:03:29,980
improve our performance and get better and better at what we do. Fifth, ratings, rankings and labels

27
00:03:31,340 --> 00:03:37,100
actually detract from performance. They don't create it. They take away from performance. And yet,

28
00:03:38,140 --> 00:03:45,980
personalized actions that help each one of us grow. Grow in our skills, grow in our attributes,

29
00:03:45,980 --> 00:03:54,940
grow in the industry or the function that we are in. When we focus on these personalized actions,

30
00:03:54,940 --> 00:04:03,660
we become better and better. And the sixth and final truth, well-being drives performance. When we are

31
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:10,620
physically healthy, mentally energized, emotionally fulfilled and grounded to a higher purpose, not just

32
00:04:10,620 --> 00:04:17,340
individually, but collectively, we lay the grounds for consistent great performance.

